// Otomo's mapping of Karoryfer Growlybass (CC0), played in place of
// growlybass_clean.sfz: the same sustained samples, with two fixes.
//
// - Keys are where the notes sound. The library maps each sample an octave
//   above its pitch (bass parts are written an octave up), so General MIDI
//   parts came out an octave low and E1-G#1 had no sample at all. The range
//   also stretches the top sample up instead of hitting the pick scrapes.
// - Every sample is brought to the same level (RMS of its first 0.85 s at
//   -27.8 dBFS, before the catalog's gain), and velocity follows sfizz's
//   default curve, as the SoundFont does. The library's own levels jumped
//   by up to 5 dB between layers - softer at f than at mf on some notes -
//   and by as much between neighbouring notes.

